            <p class="c0">Project: <b>Puzzle Race Bot</b></p>
            <p class="c0">My most memorable moment was when the bot successfully hosted its very first full race. Before that, our team had spent days preprocessing more than 2 million data records and loading them into SQLite. When I typed the command !puzzle_race 100 3, the bot instantly responded with a sharp image. The entire chat room fell silent. Seconds later, a teammate submitted the correct answer, a “ding” notification popped up, and the bot confirmed the result and updated the scoreboard. The race was incredibly exciting.</p>
            <p class="c0">The biggest challenge—and the most interesting one—was ensuring transaction integrity in an asynchronous environment. Imagine the bot receiving tokens from 10 players but crashing before the race ends or rewards are given—where would the tokens go? Losing user tokens was unacceptable. To solve this, I designed a solid transaction logging system directly on the MessageDatabase (SQLite) provided by the SDK.</p>
